From d42a987cbd10016a56d5eb0aa027b7fa8227379c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:30:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] generate: STRATA_SLOT_CKPT_MOVE=1 moves a batch
 admission's turn checkpoint into the slot

A batch admission copied the main chain's longest checkpoint into the slot (~112 MB of host vectors, 7.6 ms, ~60 ms
on fresh pages).  With the switch, the request's own turn checkpoint (or one it took out of the slot it is admitted
to) moves instead; a root, a pinned prefix and any other checkpoint the chain shares are still copied.

The chain then no longer holds it, so the request path also looks in the slots:
- while the main session holds its tokens (live, its cells below it), a slot's checkpoint is restored on the main
  session as a chain one would be, with no K/V copy; when that slot is the one the request is admitted to, it moves
  back into the chain first (the admission drops the slot's checkpoints), else the slot keeps it and the admission
  copies it as it copied the chain's;
- an active slot's checkpoints are a slot source like an idle slot's (its windows write its cells from p on): a
  second request with the same history after the main session moved on restores instead of reading it all;
- a slot source that is the admit slot moves its checkpoint into the chain instead of copying it.

The switch also keeps the dropped checkpoints' storage as STRATA_CKPT_POOL=1 does: a moved checkpoint frees
nothing at the next prune, so without it every save faulted in fresh pages (17 -> 38-60 ms, more than the copy saved).

Off by default: nothing changes.  A session SAVE or a parked conversation right after an admission lacks the moved
turn checkpoint (the slot holds it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
